\chapter{Contrasting Opinions and Open Debates}
\label{app:debates}

This book is deliberately opinionated. % ← one sentence naming the book's overall stance.

This appendix is the honest counterweight: for each major position the book
takes, it lays out the strongest case \emph{against}, names where the book sits,
and flags how well that stance holds up against the evidence available right now.

Treat this as a \textbf{state-of-the-debate snapshot as of {{DATE}}}. The field
moves fast enough that several of these debates will have shifted by the time you
read this --- which is why each section ends with the open question rather than a
settled verdict. Sources are tiered in prose so you can weight them yourself:

\textbf{T1} is a peer-reviewed paper or first-party lab report;
\textbf{T2} is vendor or first-party material with a commercial stake in the
conclusion (weigh accordingly);
\textbf{T3} is a practitioner essay.
The \emph{verdict flags} (\emph{well-supported} / \emph{contested} / \emph{dated})
are the book's self-assessment of its own position, not a claim of absolute truth.

